    simpleos_freestanding_kernel_elf32_wrap_and_weak_gate_overbroad_2026-08-06, 0, "Two root causes fixed (ELF64 + weak gate); root cause #3 remains open in the guest lexer/parser dispatch path"
    simpleos_freestanding_kernel_elf32_wrap_and_weak_gate_overbroad_2026-08-06, 1, "Triage 2026-11-04: root causes 1 and 2 fixed; open part is root cause 3 (in-guest hello.spl rc=70, str.clear receiver=0x0) which needs a rebuilt kernel plus guest simple through the OVMF-pflash board-proxy pipeline; not reproducible on this Windows host without that lane. Premise may be stale: the interpreter/seed was redeployed 2026-11-04 (0b2c3d015b7). QUESTION: is there a current SimpleOS guest image build to re-run the rc=70 probe on, or should this be set to verification-pending against the next kernel build?"

